notes:
Was 13/20. The failures were STEP-CAP, not wrong answers: plain lex-DFS hits
811,418 iterations worst case against 112,018 on the worst public case, and no
per-iteration cost fits 15M ticks.

Fixed by replacing the search, not the machine. Meet-in-the-middle with the right
half fixed at 8 indices, so hL = n-8 is the only geometry derived from n. Cost is
2^hL * (2^hR + 1) = 1,052,672 comparisons at n=20 REGARDLESS of input. Lex order
is free: left masks walked by a counter counting down, so the peeled mask is
bitrev(counter), which visits index sets in exactly lexicographic order.

True ceiling MEASURED, not sampled: 20 even values with an odd target (nothing
satisfiable, every one of 4096 left masks tried against all 257 words of ring B)
= 6,329,954 ticks, 42% of the cap. Cost is flat in the input beyond n, so that
bounds any private case.

Server ticks ran 2.73x local (798,378 vs 292,147) — the largest inflation we have
measured; pathfinder was 1.31x, matmul 1.49x, reverse-a-list 1.56x.

Routing rule that unblocked the layout: two corridors may cross freely at a BLANK,
but never at a turn glyph. Recorded in _scan's docstring.
